        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:27",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And hast not suffered me to kiss my sons and my daughters? thou hast now done foolishly in so doing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:28",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "It is in the power of my hand to do you hurt: but the God of your father spake unto me yesternight, saying, Take thou heed that thou speak not to Jacob either good or bad.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:29",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, though thou wouldest needs be gone, because thou sore longedst after thy father’s house, yet wherefore hast thou stolen my gods?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 101
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:30",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jacob answered and said to Laban, Because I was afraid: for I said, Peradventure thou wouldest take by force thy daughters from me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:31",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "With whomsoever thou findest thy gods, let him not live: before our brethren discern thou what is thine with me, and take it to thee. For Jacob knew not that Rachel had stolen them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 97
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 124
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:32",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "And Laban went into Jacob’s tent, and into Leah’s tent, and into the two maidservants’ tents; but he found them not. Then went he out of Leah’s tent, and entered into Rachel’s tent.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 111
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:33",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "Now Rachel had taken the images, and put them in the camel’s furniture, and sat upon them. And Laban searched all the tent, but found them not.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 134,
            "end": 138
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:34",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "And she said to her father, Let it not displease my lord that I cannot rise up before thee; for the custom of women is upon me. And he searched, but found not the images.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 118
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 35,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:35",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 35
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jacob was wroth, and chode with Laban: and Jacob answered and said to Laban, What is my trespass? what is my sin, that thou hast so hotly pursued after me?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 88
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 109
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 36,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:36",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 36
      },
      {
        "text": "Whereas thou hast searched all my stuff, what hast thou found of all thy household stuff? set it here before my brethren and thy brethren, that they may judge betwixt us both.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 37,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 31:37",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 31,
        "verse": 37
      },
      {
